{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom flow_autotts.controllers.optimal import OptimalController\nfrom flow_autotts.core.env import FlowTTSEnv\nfrom flow_autotts.core.model_api import IdentityVAE\n\nclass ToyModel:\n    def velocity(self, z, t, condition=None):\n        return tuple(1.0 - x for x in z)\n\nclass ToyScorer:\n    def score(self, z1_hat, condition=None):\n        target = (0.8, 0.2)\n        value = 1.0 - sum((a-b)*(a-b) for a,b in zip(z1_hat, target))\n        return float(value), {\\\"toy\\\": float(value)}\n\ncontroller = OptimalController()\nfor beta in [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]:\n    env = FlowTTSEnv(\n        model=ToyModel(),\n        vae=IdentityVAE(),\n        scorer=ToyScorer(),\n        prompt=\\\"p\\\",\n        budget=64,\n        time_grid=[i/10 for i in range(11)],\n        seed=0,\n        latent_shape=(2,),\n    )\n    answer = controller.solve(env, beta)\n    state = env.get_state()\n    counts = {}\n    for event in answer.event_log:\n        counts[event.action] = counts.get(event.action, 0) + 1\n    print('beta', beta, 'nfe', answer.nfe_used, 'rule', answer.rule, 'reward', round(answer.reward or 0.0, 4), 'counts', counts)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"beta 0.0 nfe 10 rule best_preview_score reward 0.9674 counts {'SPAWN': 1, 'FORWARD': 7, 'PREVIEW': 3, 'ANSWER': 1}\nbeta 0.25 nfe 20 rule best_preview_score reward 0.9674 counts {'SPAWN': 1, 'FORWARD': 10, 'PREVIEW': 10, 'ANSWER': 1}\nbeta 0.5 nfe 36 rule best_preview_score reward 0.9674 counts {'SPAWN': 1, 'FORWARD': 26, 'PREVIEW': 10, 'PRUNE': 2, 'BACKWARD': 1, 'ANSWER': 1}\nbeta 0.75 nfe 48 rule best_preview_score reward 0.9665 counts {'SPAWN': 1, 'FORWARD': 35, 'PREVIEW': 13, 'PRUNE': 2, 'BACKWARD': 2, 'ANSWER': 1}\nbeta 1.0 nfe 64 rule best_preview_score reward 0.9889 counts {'SPAWN': 1, 'FORWARD': 44, 'PREVIEW': 20, 'PRUNE': 2, 'BACKWARD': 2, 'ANSWER': 1}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new proposal in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py).\n\n**Idea**\n- Low beta stays on the strong `single-root preview` family instead of spending width where it was already winning.\n- Mid/high beta switches to `scout -> commit -> rival check -> dual-anchor repair -> tail -> fill-to-target`.\n- The new mechanism is not a threshold tweak: when late evidence is ambiguous, it repairs from both the best and runner-up anchors, then uses late confirmation previews to spend the remaining target budget only where the score gap or uncertainty says more evidence is still useful.\n\n**What I inspected**\n- `flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md`\n- Context pack tables: target curve, historical best near target, recent frontier comparison, beta opportunities, regression ledger, rejected `r0001`, historical action effects\n- Latest frontier rows from `r0004`:  \n  `beta=0.00` reward `0.787971`, NFE `10.000`  \n  `beta=0.25` reward `0.817857`, NFE `20.000`  \n  `beta=0.50` reward `0.837384`, NFE `36.000`  \n  `beta=0.75` reward `0.840149`, NFE `47.430`  \n  `beta=1.00` reward `0.843016`, NFE `63.554`\n- Beta-matched ODE rows: `0.00/0.25/0.50` were already above baseline; `0.75/1.00` were still below baseline.\n- Recent snapshots: `r0004`, `r0003`, `r0000` controllers. The last two proposals were real but mostly the same scaffold with small late-allocation changes; they did not introduce a meaningfully different repair policy.\n\n**Beta Schedule**\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: 1 root, exact single-root ladder, `7` forward + `3` preview.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: 1 root, exact single-root ladder, `10` forward + `10` preview.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: 4 roots, Euler scouts to `0.3`, keep `2`, commit to `0.7`, rival check to `0.9`, at most 1 repaired anchor with 1 child, tail to `1.0`, fill with selective confirmations/steps.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: 5 roots, 1 SDE scout, keep `3`, commit `0.7`, rival `0.9`, repair both top anchors if ambiguous, 1 child each, then late confirmation fill.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: 6 roots, 1 SDE scout, keep `4`, same stages as `0.75` but more conservative pruning and larger fill-confirmation cap.\n- Monotonicity comes from `_target_nfe` plus beta-increasing width, survivor counts, rival rounds, and late confirmation allowance.\n- `beta=1.0` cannot exceed `64` because every spend path is gated by `_can_spend(...)`, which caps against `min(schedule[\"target_nfe\"], env.budget, initial_budget)`, and termination uses `answer(\"best_preview_score\")` so there is no implicit auto-finish overshoot.\n\n**Behavioral Novelty**\n- Exact low-beta target-locked single-root ladders instead of reusing the high-beta brancher everywhere.\n- Dual-anchor repair: refine both the leader and runner-up when the late gap is small or uncertainty is high, rather than repairing only one chosen anchor.\n- Fill-to-target confirmation: if the top gap is still weak late, spend remaining budget on repeated late previews of the top few candidates before taking extra forward steps.\n\n**Target-NFE Reflection**\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: underuse is not justified here; I made it exact at `10`.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: underuse is not justified here; I made it exact at `20`.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: prior single-root behavior was already fine, but this level can support selective branching without wasting budget; the policy is shaped to use the full target with one bounded repair path.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: this was the clearest weak regime and slightly under target; I added explicit repair and fill so it should stay close to `48` instead of stopping around `47.4`.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: also weak and slightly under target; I increased late confirmation/repair opportunity while keeping the hard `64` cap.\n\n**Checks**\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- Toy `FlowTTSEnv` dry-run across all betas. Observed NFE was exactly `10/20/36/48/64`, with branching appearing only from `beta=0.5` upward and no budget overshoot.\n\n**Expected Risks**\n- `beta=0.50` may regress slightly if branching is worse than the previous strong single-root ranking on this dataset.\n- Repeated late previews can still spend NFE on noisy anchors if PickScore variance is high.\n- The single SDE scout at `0.75/1.0` is intentionally bounded, but it could still be neutral or mildly harmful if stochastic diversity does not help enough.\n\nThis round is mainly targeting `beta=0.75` and `beta=1.0`, while protecting the already-strong `beta=0.00` and `0.25` regimes and keeping `beta=0.50` near target compute."}}
